    "q-101703": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101703",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $\\frac{c}{7}=-15,$ then $c=$",
      "worked_solution": "In the equation, $c$ is being divided by $7.$ To isolate $c$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $7.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $7.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{7} & =-15 \\\\ 7\\cdot \\frac{c}{7} & =7\\cdot (-15) \\\\ \\frac{7c}{7} & =-105\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $7$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7c}{7} & =-105 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7}c}{\\cancel{7}} & =-105 \\\\ c & =-105\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-101703-a",
