    "q-185208": {
      "dom_id": "step-q185208",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $4=\\frac{x}{6},$ then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{6}=4\n$$\n\nIn this equation, $x$ is being divided by $6.$ To isolate $x$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $6.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $6$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{6} & =4 \\\\ 6\\cdot \\frac{x}{6} & =6\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{6x}{6} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{6}x}{\\cancel{6}} & =24 \\\\ x & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
