    "q-185213": {
      "dom_id": "step-q185213",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $-5=\\frac{t}{4},$ then $t=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\frac{t}{4}=-5\n$$\n\nIn this equation, $t$ is being divided by $4.$ To isolate $t$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $4.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $4$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{t}{4} & =-5 \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{t}{4} & =4\\cdot (-5) \\\\ \\frac{4t}{4} & =-20 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}t}{\\cancel{4}} & =-20 \\\\ t & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
