    "q-6233": {
      "dom_id": "step-q6233",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "If $-\\frac{x}{7}=-3,$ then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's remove the negative sign from the variable. To do this, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{x}{7} & =-3 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{7}) & =(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ \\frac{x}{7} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the equation above, $x$ is being *divided* by $7.$ To isolate $x$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $7.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $7$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{7} & =3 \\\\ 7\\cdot \\frac{x}{7} & =7\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & =21 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7}x}{\\cancel{7}} & =21 \\\\ x & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
