    "q-104729": {
      "dom_id": "step-q104729",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "If $-8x=-56$, then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "The variable $x$ is being *multiplied* by $-8.$ To isolate $x$, we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-8.$ So, we divide both sides of the equation by $-8.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8x & =-56 \\\\ \\frac{-8x}{-8} & =\\frac{-56}{-8} \\\\ \\frac{-8x}{-8} & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-8$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8x}{-8} & =7 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-8}x}{\\cancel{-8}} & =7 \\\\ x & =7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
